Third-party material

- The repository layout, the judge tooling under tools/bac, the workflows and the shared
  documents under spec/ are adapted from the Quantum Autoresearch Challenge
  (https://github.com/teddyjfpender/quantum-autoresearch-challenge), Apache-2.0.
- challenges/binohash/benchmark.sh and the two-process build/evaluate design are adapted,
  through that repository, from the ecdsa.fail point-addition challenge
  (https://github.com/Layr-Labs/ecdsafail-challenge).
- The Binohash construction, its parameters and the script listings the baseline builder
  follows are from R. Linus, "Binohash: Transaction Introspection Without Softforks" (2026),
  https://robinlinus.com/binohash.pdf. They are cited in challenges/binohash/spec/REFERENCES.md.
- challenges/binohash/evaluator/bh/ripemd160.py is a pure-Python RIPEMD-160 used only where
  hashlib does not provide one.
- challenges/binohash/tools/core links the Rust crate `bitcoinconsensus`, which packages the
  consensus library of Bitcoin Core (MIT).
- Evidence levels and cost boundaries in challenges/binohash/spec/CONVENTIONS.md follow the
  bitcoin-scripts knowledge base (https://github.com/solving-bitcoin/bitcoin-scripts).

If you are an author of reused material and want the attribution changed, write to the
